{
  "id": "COMPOUND:16590 - PROTEIN:2333",
  "verbalization": "Gerontoisoflavone A appears to interact with Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3 through a series of indirect pathways, with the target enzyme being shared across multiple molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Gerontoisoflavone A acts as a target for several molecules, including methyl 2-[(1R,2R)-2-[(Z)-5-hydroxypent-2-enyl]-3-oxocyclopentyl]acetate, 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline, and Dual specificity protein kinase CLK2. These molecules, in turn, are targets of the enzyme Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3, indicating a potential regulatory role for the latter in the activation or inhibition of these downstream targets. The shared involvement of Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3 in the pathways of Gerontoisoflavone A suggests a possible functional link, possibly through the modulation of signaling cascades or the regulation of protein activity. The evidence supports a mechanism where Gerontoisoflavone A may influence the activity of Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
